From dcf5e98017c62c89332bcafa2a392830e9f913e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grizbeard <justin.morken@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 13:33:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] Let a skin opt out of cue and track colours, and do it
 in the mono schemes

Cue colours and track colours come from the user's colour palette, so they
bear no relation to the skin's. A scheme with several hues absorbs them; a
single-hue one has nowhere to put them, and a stray orange hotcue was then
the only colour on a monochrome screen.

Four places paint them, and they needed three different answers.

The track colour washed over a library row is already a skin setting --
<TrackTableBackgroundColorOpacity>, 0.175 here -- so the monochrome
schemes set it to 0. No core change at all. The colour column proper is
painted straight onto the viewport by ColorDelegate, which reads
mixxxColorDelegateUseRowBackgroundForColorCell off the table view first,
so the stylesheet sets that too; the column is not in the default layout,
so that half is set but was not exercised.

The other two do need core support, added as a widget option in the same
vein as the DimBrightThreshold and Hover already on these widgets:

- <UseCueColor>false</UseCueColor> on a HotcueButton stops it injecting
  the cue's colour as its own stylesheet, so the skin's qss styles it like
  any other latched button. The light/dark hints it publishes for qss are
  suppressed with it, since they describe a colour no longer in play.
- The same on a <Mark> or <DefaultMark> keeps the <Color> the skin
  declared instead of adopting the cue's. Cue colours now arrive through
  WaveformMark::setCueColor, which is the one place that decision is made;
  the waveform and the overview both go through it.

Both default to true, so every other skin is unaffected, and Btop keeps
its colours.

Verified with a hotcue set on a loaded track: the button is #ff8000 under
Btop and #33ff3a under Green Phosphor, and the waveform strip holds 366
cue-coloured pixels under Btop against none under Green Phosphor. With a
track coloured red, its library row is washed #2d0000 under Btop and is
left black under Green Phosphor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
